===Etymology 1===
The {{glossary|noun}} is an {{initialism|en|deoxyribonucleic acid|nocap=1}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=56224|date=September 2022|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from the noun.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|genetics}}{{lb|en|biochemistry|genetics}} {{initialism of|en|deoxyribonucleic acid|t=a [[nucleic acid]] [[find#Verb|found]] in all [[living thing]]s (and some [[non-living]] things such as certain [[virus#Noun|viruses]]) which [[consist#Verb|consists]] of [[two]] [[polynucleotide]] [[chain#Noun|chains]] that [[coil#Verb|coil]] around each other to [[form#Verb|form]] a [[double#Adjective|double]] [[helix#Noun|helix]]; [[encode#Verb|encoded]] in its [[structure#Noun|structure]] are [[genetic]] [[instruction]]s for [[development]], [[functioning#Noun|functioning]], [[growth]], and [[reproduction]]}}
# {{lb|en|informal|loosely}} The [[part#Noun|part]] of a living thing that [[carry#Verb|carries]] genetic [[information]].
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} The [[fundamental#Adjective|fundamental]] [[nature#Noun|nature]] or [[value#Noun|values]] of a [[person#Noun|person]], or an [[organization]] or other thing, especially when [[consider]]ed as [[innate]] and/or [[unchangeable]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Kevin John Kennedy|author2=Mary Moore|title=Going the Distance|publisher=FT Press|year=2003|isbn=9780130461209|page={{gbooks|tgdyUfysdJ8C|14}}|passage=These ingredients in a  company's '''DNA''' mean that company will attract and grow leaders with these qualities.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Bill McBean|title=The Facts of Business Life|publisher=John Wiley & Sons|year=2012|isbn=9781118236994|passage=The main leadership priority at Level 2 is creating the business's '''DNA''' by defining how all the moving parts of the company will work, both independently and  together.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ryan Bort|title=The Real Reason Republicans Are Loading Their 2022 Campaign Ads With Guns|journal={{w|Rolling Stone}}|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/guns-republican-primary-campaign-ads-midterms-1336903/|date=2022-04-13|passage=It’s coming from the hardcore MAGA set, and not only is it likely to stick around beyond the primaries, it’s likely hardwired into the '''DNA''' of a party now driven by extremism, conspiracy, and a belief that violence is a legitimate tool to achieve desired political outcomes.}}

